---
title: Chapatis
description: Traditional unleavened Indian flatbread
yield: 10
course: Side
prep time: 20m
cook time: 10m
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: Indian
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- bread
- indian
- vegetarian
- side-dish
- savoury
---

Mix the @chapati flour{280%g}(or 50/50 mix of plain and wholemeal flour) and @salt{1%tsp} in a large bowl. Stir in the @olive oil{2%tbsp} and enough @hot water{180%ml}(or as needed) to make a soft dough that is elastic but not sticky.

Knead the dough on a lightly floured surface for 5 to ~{10%minutes} until it is smooth. Divide into 10 pieces, or fewer for bigger breads. Roll each piece into a ball, and let them rest for a few minutes.

Heat a #frying pan{} over medium heat until hot, and grease lightly with @olive oil{}. On a lightly floured surface, use a floured #rolling pin{} to roll out the balls of dough until very thin like a tortilla.

When the pan starts smoking, put a chapati on it. Cook until the underside has brown spots, about ~{30%seconds}, then flip and cook on the other side. Put on a plate and keep warm while cooking the rest of the chapatis.